$comments
the diagonal corresponds to the energy level of each point. Then, each other
edge corresponds to the weight. The way graph is implemented, the probability
of picking a neighbour is $A_{ij}/sum_{k=0, k\neq i}^{n-1}A_{ij}$. So if 
you replace each 0.5 with a 1.0 above then it will work just fine.

The code will take in either a score matrix or an edge_weight matrix. 
Note this is a directed graph, so you have to include both $a->b$ and $b->a$.
lines that say $a->a$ are treated as the energy of the graph.
Also, it looks for "$begin_edge_weights" at the start of the line: any extra
garbage at the end is not processed. Same with all lines.
